From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ucm2: Qualcomm: eliza: match the CQS EVK by its card name

The EVK configuration is reached through
conf.d/eliza/eliza-cqs-evk.conf, which alsa-lib looks up by the card
long name. The long name equals the card name ("eliza-cqs-evk", the
model of the DT sound node) only when the boot firmware provides no
SMBIOS tables; otherwise ASoC builds it from DMI. Under U-Boot the EVK
reports board vendor "qcom" and product " Inc. Eliza CQS EVK", so the
long name is "qcom-Inc.ElizaCQSEVK" and no configuration is found
("failed to import hw:0 use case configuration -2").

Add the driver level conf.d/eliza/eliza.conf, which alsa-lib tries
next, and pick the EVK configuration there by the card name, which
does not depend on the firmware.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ucm2/Qualcomm/eliza/eliza.conf | 14 ++++++++++++++
 ucm2/conf.d/eliza/eliza.conf   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ucm2/Qualcomm/eliza/eliza.conf
 create mode 120000 ucm2/conf.d/eliza/eliza.conf

diff --git a/ucm2/Qualcomm/eliza/eliza.conf b/ucm2/Qualcomm/eliza/eliza.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..358cc6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ucm2/Qualcomm/eliza/eliza.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+Syntax 4
+
+# The card long name is built from DMI when the boot firmware provides
+# SMBIOS tables, so it depends on the firmware; the card name is the
+# model of the DT sound node.
+
+If.cqsevk {
+	Condition {
+		Type String
+		String1 "${CardName}"
+		String2 "eliza-cqs-evk"
+	}
+	True.Include.evk.File "/Qualcomm/eliza/eliza-cqs-evk/eliza-cqs-evk.conf"
+}
diff --git a/ucm2/conf.d/eliza/eliza.conf b/ucm2/conf.d/eliza/eliza.conf
new file mode 120000
index 0000000..013a8fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ucm2/conf.d/eliza/eliza.conf
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+../../Qualcomm/eliza/eliza.conf
\ No newline at end of file
-- 
2.53.0

